$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: N -Acetyl rotaxane 2 A solution of 1 (98 mg,
0.10 mmol), acetic anhydride (19 mL, 0.20 mmol), and triethylamine (70
mL, 0.50 mmol) in N,N-dimethylformamide (0.80 ml) was stirred at 40 °C
for 24 h. The reaction mixture was diluted by dichloromethane, washed by
1 M hydrochloric acid followed by saturated sodium carbonate solution,
dried over magnesium sulfate, and evaporated in vacuo. The crude product
was purified by preparative GPC to give 80 mg (91 %) of 2 as white solid.
2 white solid. m.p. 157 °C. 1H NMR (270 MHz, CDCl3, 423 K) δ 8.01 (d, J =
7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.93 (s, 2H), 7.09 (s, 1H), 6.91-6.74 (m, 13H), 5.93 (s,
2H), 4.34 (s, 2H), 4.30 (s, 2H), 4.11-3.96 (m, 8H), 3.72-3.65 (m, 4H),
3.60-3.53 (m, 4H), 3.37-3.28 (m, 4H), 3.17-3.09 (m, 4H), 2.24 (s, 6H),
2.20 (s, 6H), 2.01 (s, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (125.7 MHz, CDCl3, 298 K) δ
166.94, 166.92, 148.37, 148.31, 138.34, 137.86, 137.56, 137.49, 137.40,
137.23, 136.65, 136.60, 134.24, 133.98, 133.92, 133.62, 130.74, 130.71,
129.27, 128.93, 128.90, 128.78, 128.14, 126.66, 125.99, 125.44, 123.97,
120.40, 120.36, 111.41, 111.39, 69.56, 69.53, 69.36, 69.30, 67.86, 66.90,
66.78, 50.71, 50.09, 47.60, 47.48, 21.82, 21.68, 21.39, 21.36, 20.89 ppm.
FAB-MS (m-NBA matrix) m/z 878.5 [M]+. IR (νeat) 1710 (ν C=O ester), 1639
(ν C=O amide) cm-1. Anal, calcd for C52H63NO11: C, 71.13; H, 7.23; N,
1.60. found: C, 71.02; H, 7.35; N, 1.60.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
