$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for parallel synthesis of
ureidothiophene carboxylic acid library: In a typical run, we realized
the reactions with 8 thiaisatoic anhydrides A{1-19} and 10 amines
B{1-60}. In a crystallizing dish intended to one selected amine, we
disposed 1 mmole of each of the eight anhydrides in 8 glass jars. Water
(10 ml) was added to give an aqueous suspension of thiaisatoic anhydride
and efficient magnetic stirring was performed. The addition of 2.2 mmoles
of primary or secondary amines allowed the quick apparition of a
solution. Magnetic stirring was pursued for 2 hours. About 5ml of a 37%
hydrochloric acid solution were then added, the precipitate which was
formed was filtered off and washed with water to give ureidothiophene
carboxylic acids. Analysis by 1H NMR and LC/MS identified successful
reaction. -a6-b2-carbonylaminothiophene-2-carboxylic acid A6B2
C14H13FN2O3S 308.33 g.mol-1 1H NMR : = 1.1 (t, 3JHH = 7.2 Hz, 3H, CH3),
3.1 (q, 3JHH = 7.2 Hz, 2H, CH2), 7.3 (t, 3JHH and HF = 8.7 Hz, 2H, Har),
7.6 (broad s, 1H, NH), 7.7 (dd, 3JHH = 8.7 Hz and 4JHF = 5.6 Hz, 2H,
Har), 8.2 (s, 1H, Hthiophene), 9.3 (broad s, 1H, NH), 12.04 (broad s, 1H,
COOH)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM combinatorial, solution phase synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solution-phase parallel synthesis of a 1140-member ureidothiophene
carboxylic acid library
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Le Foulon, Francois-Xavier; Braud, Emmanuelle; Fabis, Frederic; Lancelot,
Jean-Charles; Rault, Sylvain
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Combinatorial Chemistry (2005), 7(2), 253-257

