$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for catalyst recovery In a
dry 250-mL, two-necked, round-bottomed flask was placed MoO2Cl2 (100 mg,
0.5 mmol) in 50 mL of anhydrous solvent (CH2Cl2 was used unless it is
stated otherwise). To the above solution, anhydride (75 mmol) was slowly
added at ambient temperature. After for 30 min, a solution of nucleophile
(50 mmol in CH2Cl2, 20 mL) was slowly added to the above bluish solution
and the reaction mixture was stirred for indicated time periods. After
completion of the reaction as monitored by TLC, the reaction mixture was
quenched with ice-cold water (100 mL). The separated aqueous layer was
concentrated by rotatory evaporator at 40 °C. Subsequently, the recovered
catalyst was dried in vacuo at ambient temperature for 2 hours to get
bluish solid (100 mg) in essentially quantitative recovery. (S)-Methyl
2-Acetylamino-3, 3-dimethyl-butanoate53 Data: 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3)
5.97 (bs, 1H), 4.48 (d, J = 9.4, 1H), 3.72 (s, 3H), 2.03 (s, 3H), 0.97
(s, 9H); 13C NMR (50 MHz, CDCl3) 172.30, 169.88, 59.78, 51.56, 34.41,
26.31, 22.96; TLC Rf 0.25 (EtOAc/hexane, 1/10).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM catalyst may be recovered
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nucleophilic acyl substitutions of anhydrides with protic nucleophiles
catalyzed by amphoteric, oxomolybdenum species
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
