$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for acylation of
tert-butanol and trityl alcohol In a dry 50-mL, two-necked,
round-bottomed flask was placed MoO2Cl2 (19 mg, 0.1 mmol) in 5 mL of
anhydrous toluene. A solution of anhydride (15 mmol) and a given 3o
alcohol (10 mmol) in toluene (5 mL) was slowly added to the above
solution and the reaction mixture was stirred for 30 min to 1 hour. To
the above solution, diisopropylethylamine (1750 μL, 10 mmol) was slowly
added at ambient temperature. This mixture was refluxed for 1 to 24
hours. After completion of the reaction as monitored by TLC (for the
benzoylation of tryl alcohol), the reaction mixture was quenched with
cold, saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution (50 mL) at room temperature. The
separated organic layer was washed with brine, dried (MgSO4), filtered,
and evaporated. The crude product was purified by distillation. The
product obtained was characterized by routine spectroscopic methods
N-tert-Butyl-2,2-dimethyl-propionamide39 Data: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
5.38 (bs, 1H), 1.32 (s, 9H), 1.14 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3)
177.77, 50.64, 38.94, 28.71, 27.64; TLC Rf 0.45 (EtOAc/hexane, 1/4).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM catalyst may be recovered
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nucleophilic acyl substitutions of anhydrides with protic nucleophiles
catalyzed by amphoteric, oxomolybdenum species
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
