$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for the Acetylation
2-Naphthol (0.720 g, 5 mmol) was treated with Ac2O (0.48 mL, 5 mmol)
under neat conditions at rt for 30 min under magnetic stirring in the
presence of SO42-/SnO2 (0.5 mol%) with respect to substrate. The course
of the reaction was monitored by thin-layer chromatography (TLC) and gas
chromatography (GC). The reaction mixture was diluted with Et2O (20 mL),
and the solution was filtered to separate the catalyst. The filtrate was
washed successively with 1% aqueous NaOH (15 mL) and brine (15 mL), dried
(Na2SO4), and concentrated to afford the product, which was in full
agreement with the mp and spectral data (IR, 1H NMR) of an authentic
sample of 2-acetoxynaphthalene (0.883 g, 95% with SO42-/ SnO2). The
catalyst was recovered and reused for a fresh lot of
2-hydroxynaphthalene. Table 2., Entry 17, Yield 94% Bp (Torr) or mp (°C)
Found 61 Reported 61[14]
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry (- catalyst), sulfated tin oxide used as catalyst, no
solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM SO42-/SnO2: Efficient, chemoselective, and reusable catalyst for
acylation of alcohols, phenols, and amines at room temperature
