$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of N-Butanoyl-4-methyl
Benzenesulfonamide: A Typical Procedure for NAcylation of Sulfonamides
under Solvent-free Conditions: To a vigorously stirred mixture of
4-methyl benzenesulfonamide (0.342 g, 2 mmol) and P2O5/SiO2 [(w/w 75%),
0.35 g], butanoic anhydride (0.632 g, 4 mmol) was added in two portions
at 80 °C. The progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC. After the
completion of the reaction, ethyl acetate (20 ml) was added and the solid
materials were removed by filtration. The filtrate was washed with water
(15 ml) and dried over MgSO4. After evaporation of the solvent, the crude
product was purified by recrystallization from toluene or ethyl
acetate/n-hexane mixed solvent to afford Nbutanoyl-4-methyl
benzenesulfonamide. Yield 98%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-catalyst, green chemistry-process simplification,
solid-supported catalyst, silica-supported P2O5 prepared and used as
catalyst, catalyst recyclable, alternatively reaction carried out using
dichloromethane as solvent, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM P2O5/SiO2 as an efficient and recyclable catalyst for N-acylation of
sulfonamides under heterogeneous and solvent-free conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Massah, A. R.; Dabagh, M.; Shahidi, S.; Naghash, H. Javaherian; Momeni,
A. R.; Aliyan, H.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the Iranian Chemical Society (2009), 6(2), 405-411

