$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 1343-93-7
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Synthesis of Acyclic Imides by the Reaction of
Liquid Aliphatic Nitriles with Aliphatic Anhydrides in the Presence of
H3PW12O40 under Thermal Conditions and MW Irradiation A mixture of
nitrile (20 mmol), aliphatic anhydride (1 mmol) and H3PW12O40 (0.055
mmol) was heated at 70 °C or irradiated under MW (800 W) at 40 °C (the
total volume was less than 1 ml). The reaction progress was monitored by
GC. After completion of the reaction, the mixture was cooled to room
temperature and Et2O (15 ml) was added. The catalyst was filtered and
washed with Et2O (10 ml). The filtrates were concentrated and the crude
product was purified by chromatography on a short column of silica-gel
(ethyl acetate: petroleum ether, 1:3) to obtain the pure product (Table
2). N-Acetylacetamide (Table 2, entry 1), White solid, Yield 97% m.p.: 73
°C. IR (KBr) νmax 3270, 3120, 2991, 1738, 1550, 1240 cm-1. 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.31 (6H, s, 2CH3), 8.63 (1H, br s, NH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-process simplification, microwave irradiation (800 W),
lower yield for thermal conditions, catalyst recovery and reuse,
optimization study, optimized on catalyst, amount of catalyst, amount of
nitrile, temperature, time and mode of conditions, low conversion without
catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient synthesis of symmetrical and unsymmetrical acyclic imides
catalyzed by reusable 12-tungstophosphoric acid under thermal conditions
and microwave irradiation
