$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Liquid Nitriles A mixture of 50 mmol of nitrile,
silica sulfuric acid (0.18 g, equal to 1.36 mmol H+) and 1 mmol of
carboxylic anhydride was heated in a 25 mL round-bottomed flask at 60-70
°C. The reactions were completed within 6-8 h as monitored by TLC
(eluent, EtOAc-PE, 1:1). The mixture was filtered and solvent was
evaporated under reduced pressure. A solution of NaHCO3 in H2O (1%, 10
mL) was added and the mixture was extracted with Et2O (3 × 25 mL). The
organic layer was separated and dried over Na2SO4. When necessary, the
crude product was purified by preparative TLC on silica gel.
N-Acetylacetamide (entry 1): white solid, yield 96%. Mp 73-74 °C. 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 2.07 (s, 6 H), 8.72 (br s, 1 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 24.91, 171.96. IR (KBr): 3410, 3265, 3215, 1732 cm-1. MS
(EI): m/z (rel. intensity) = 101 (10) [M+], 72 (35), 58 (100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM cat. recyclable, 5 runs yield was 75%
