$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):CAT(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7718-54-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure A mixture of aliphatic and
aromatic compounds containing alcohols, amines, phenols, or thiols
(2mmol), 3-4 mmol acetic anhydride (Ac2O), and 0.1mol% (13 mg) anhydrous
nickel chloride (NiCl2) was stirred magnetically at room temperature, and
the progress of the reaction was monitored by thin-layer chromatography
(TLC). The reaction mixture was diluted with water (30 ml) and extracted
with chloroform (3 x 30 ml). The combined chloroform extracts were washed
successively with 10% sodium bicarbonate and water, dried with Na2SO4,
and concentrated under reduced pressure. In all the cases, the product
obtained after the usual workup gave satisfactory spectral data.
N,N-Diethyl Ethanamide (28b), yield 97% IR (KBr): 855, 915, 1010, 1125,
1410, 1750, 2947, 3025 cm-1; 1HNMR (300MHz, CDCl2): δ = 0.9 (t, 6H, 2 x
CH3); 1.4 (q, 4H, 2 x CH2); 2.5 (s, 3H, COCH3). Anal, calcd. for C6H13ON:
C, 62.57; H, 11.37; N, 12.16. Found: C, 62.56; H, 11.36; N, 12.15.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Simple and efficient method for acetylation of alcohols, phenols, amines,
and thiols using anhydrous NiCl2 under solvent-free conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Meshram, G. A.; Patil, V. D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2009), 39(14), 2516-2528

