$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical Procedure: A mixture of phthalic anhydride (1.48 g, 10 mmol) and
formamide (1.36g, 30 mmol) was introduced in a 100-mL flask fitted with a
water condenser out of the cavity through an adaptor and then subjected
to microwave irradiation (400 W) for 2 min. After completion of the
reaction, 10 mL of hot water was added and the crude product was
separated by filtration. The solid thus obtained recrystallized from
ethanol to give 1.43 g (97% yield) of phthalimide as colorless needles.
Table: Entry 1, yield 1.43 g (97%). M.P. (°C) Obs, Lit.: 239-240, 23814
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Imidation of cyclic carboxylic anhydrides under microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
