$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: N,N-hexanoyltosylhydrazide (4): general
procedure of acylation with an acid anhydride To a solution of
N-tosylhydrazide 3 (50 mg, 0.27 mmol) in dichloromethane (1.3 mL) were
added triethylamine (56 mL, 0.40 mmol) and 4-aminopyridine (5.0 mg, 0.40
mmol). The mixture was cooled to 0 °C, and acetic anhydride (28 mL, 0.29
mmol) was added. The mixture was stirred for 30 min at 0 °C, quenched
with sat. aq. solution of NaHCO3, and extracted with dichloromethane (5
mL x 2). The combined organic layers were dried over anhydrous MgSO4,
filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by silica gel flash column chromatography (elution with
hexane/ethyl acetate = 10/1 to 3/1) to give 8 (74 mg, 96%) as white
crystals. N,N-hexanoyltosylhydrazide (4): white crystals. mp 91 °C
(recrystalized from hexane-ethyl acetate); IR (neat) 3389, 3315, 2957,
2931, 2871, 1689, 1453, 1349, 1168, 1134, 913, cm-1; 1HNMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.89 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.33 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 2.72 (t, J =
7.5 Hz, 2H), 2.44 (s, 3H), 1.59 (quint, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 1.23-1.33 (m,
4H), 0.87 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 3H); 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 7.84 (d, J =
8.1 Hz, 2H), 7.38 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 5.63 (s, 2H), 2.40-2.55 (m, 2H),
2.38 (s, 3H), 1.38 (quint, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 1.21-1.10 (m, 4H), 0.79 (t, J
= 7.5 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 174.7, 145.1, 134.9, 129.5,
128.7, 35.6, 31.2, 24.0, 22.4, 21.7, 13.9; HRMS (EI) m/z [M]+ calcd for
[C13H20N2O3S]+ 284.1195, found 284.1205.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, other catalyst gave slightly lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
