$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure G. Reaction of amine
compounds with acylating agents. Amine (1 equiv.) was purged with argon,
dissolved in pyridine (0.2 M), and cooled to 0 °C. Acylating agent (1
equiv.) was added, and the reaction mixture was stirred at 0 °C for 3 h.
Saturated NaHCO3 was added, and the reaction mixture was extracted with 4
x 5 mL of DCM. The combined organic layers were dried over Na2SO4 and
concentrated in vacuo. Compounds were purified using basic or acidic
conditions via preparative chromatography. Lactam 50{1}. Prepared
according to general procedure G using amine 49 (0.056 g, 0.21 mmol) and
acetic anhydride (0.061 mL, 0.64 mmol) to give the product as an oil
(0.062 g, 95%). 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.33 (dt, J = 4.4, 6.8, 3H),
7.11 (d, J = 7.0, 2H), 6.98 (s, 1H), 4.59 (s, 1H), 3.84 (dd, J = 6.6,
13.8, 1H), 3.73 (dd, J = 6.4, 13.8, 1H), 3.25 (d, J = 17.4, 1H), 3.21 (s,
3H), 2.71 (s, 3H), 2.53 (d, J = 17.4, 1H), 2.05 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (151
MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.1, 172.1, 171.4, 135.9, 129.0, 128.9, 127.6, 70.0,
54.3, 52.3, 45.3, 36.8, 28.8, 23.5; IR (neat) 3291, 2950, 1734, 1658
cm-1; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C16H21N2O4 (M + H)+ 305.1496, found
305.1498.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of a γ-Lactam Library via Formal Cycloaddition of Imines and
Substituted Succinic Anhydrides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
