$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N,N-hexanoyltosylhydrazide (4): general procedure of acylation with an
acid anhydride To a solution of N-tosylhydrazide 3 (50 mg, 0.27 mmol) in
dichloromethane (1.3 mL) were added triethylamine (56 mL, 0.40 mmol) and
4-aminopyridine (5.0 mg, 0.40 mmol). The mixture was cooled to 0 °C, and
acetic anhydride (28 mL, 0.29 mmol) was added. The mixture was stirred
for 30 min at 0 °C, quenched with sat. aq. solution of NaHCO3, and
extracted with dichloromethane (5 mL x 2). The combined organic layers
were dried over anhydrous MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced
pressure. The residue was purified by silica gel flash column
chromatography (elution with hexane/ethyl acetate = 10/1 to 3/1) to give
8 (74 mg, 96%) as white crystals. N,N-acetyltosylhydrazide (8) White
solids; mp 131 °C (recrystalized from hexane-ethyl acetate); IR (neat)
3377, 3298, 3226, 1685,1627, 1598, 1354, 1167, 901, cm-1; 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.88 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.34 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 2H), 4.38
(br s, 2H), 2.45 (s, 3H), 2.40 (s, 3H), 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 171.7,
145.2, 134.6, 129.6, 128.6, 23.9, 21.6; HRMS (EI) m/z [M]+ calcd for
[C9H12N2O3S]+ 228.0568, found 228.0570.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 4-Aminopyridine Catalyzed Direct and Regioselective Acylation of
N-Tosylhydrazide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Namba, Kosuke; Shoji, Isamu; Nishizawa, Mugio; Tanino, Keiji
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2009), 11(21), 4970-4973

